# A marketplace's digests and signature cover bytes exactly as committed.
#
# Git may rewrite text files on checkout — `core.autocrlf=true` is Git for Windows' own recommended
# default — and a rewritten byte is a different byte. Without this file, a marketplace signed on
# Linux CI fails every digest AND its index signature on such a machine, all at once, and the
# failure surfaces as "nothing here is verified" with no hint that line endings caused it.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion for every path, so the working tree always holds the
# committed bytes.
* -text
